  "response_text": "If the scheduler always picks a higher priority task, it can lead to starvation. Starvation is when a lower-priority task doesn\u2019t get to run, due to many other higher-priority processes that always go before it. The low-priority task is almost \u201cforgotten\u201d. The system in turn becomes unresponsive to these low-priority tasks, which may affect the core functionality of the system. These things might include background work, or even PendSV in our case. This loses the multitasking functionality that we implemented. This makes it not fair for the program and other lower-priority tasks.\\n",
